.Dd October 30, 2026
.Dt EMOND 8
.Os Minkar
.Sh NAME
.Nm emond
.Nd the event monitor daemon
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl d
.Op Fl r Ar rulesdir
.Op Fl e Ar eventsdir
.Op Fl c Ar clientsdir
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
takes events and acts on them as its rules say.
.Xr launchd 8
starts it when its clients directory,
.Pa /var/db/emondClients ,
is not empty; it stays while it is, and rereads its rules on
.Dv SIGHUP .
.Ss Events
When it starts,
.Nm
has a
.Li startup
event.
Clients leave events as property lists in
.Pa /var/db/emond/events :
a dictionary with the
.Li eventType
and the event's own keys; each is handled and removed.
.Ss Rules
Each property list in
.Pa /etc/emond.d/rules
is an array of rules, dictionaries with:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Li name
The rule's name, for the log.
.It Li enabled
False leaves the rule out.
.It Li eventTypes
The event types it takes.
.It Li criterion
What the event must hold: dictionaries with a
.Li key
(a dotted path into the event), an
.Li operator
.Pf ( Li Equal ,
.Li NotEqual ,
.Li Contains ,
.Li BeginsWith ,
.Li EndsWith ,
.Li GreaterThan ,
.Li LessThan ,
.Li GreaterThanOrEqual ,
.Li LessThanOrEqual ,
.Li Exists ,
.Li NotExists ;
numbers compare as numbers) and a
.Li value .
All must hold, or any with
.Li allowPartialCriterionMatch .
.It Li actions
What to do, in order: dictionaries with a
.Li type :
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Li Log
Log the
.Li message
to the system log at
.Li logLevel
.Pf ( Li Notice
by default).
.It Li RunCommand
Run
.Li command
(an absolute path) with
.Li arguments ,
as
.Li user
(root by default).
.It Li SendEmail
Mail the
.Li message
with the
.Li subject
to the
.Li recipientAddresses
through
.Xr sendmail 8 .
.El
.El
.Pp
Messages, subjects and arguments may name
.Li ${event. Ns Ar key Ns Li } ,
.Li ${builtin:now}
and
.Li ${builtin:hostname} .
.Pp
.Fl d
stays in the foreground and also writes the log to the standard error;
.Fl r ,
.Fl e
and
.Fl c
name other rules, events and clients directories.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Pa /etc/emond.d/rules
.It Pa /var/db/emond/events
.It Pa /var/db/emondClients
.It Pa /System/Library/LaunchDaemons/org.minkar.emond.plist
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr launchd 8 ,
.Xr syslog 3
